65,-77.674871,43.084361,-77.674254,43.084358,-77.67437,43.084667,3731,1020,"Albert J. and Carolie R. Simone Plaza","RIT officially dedicated the Albert J. and Carolie R. Simone Plaza and Circle near the Eastman Building, Student Alumni Union and Sentinel sculpture for President Simone and his wife, Carolie.","https://whatsinaname.rit.edu/location/1074",[1327],{"_70":1323,"_72":1328,"_45":1322,"_74":1321},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/quad_courtyard_albert_simone_plaza.jpg",{"_43":1346,"_45":1347,"_47":1348,"_49":1348,"_235":1349,"_51":1350,"_63":64,"_65":1346,"_67":1351},{"_32":684,"_39":1331},[1332],[1333,1334,1335,1336,1337],[1338,1339],[1344,1345],[1342,1343],[1340,1341],[1338,1339],-77.676427,43.084867,-77.676432,43.084659,-77.675987,43.084651,-77.675982,43.084859,3735,1021,"Eastman Kodak Quad","Eastman Kodak Quad refers to a courtyard surrounded by George Eastman Hall, Frank E. Gannett Hall, and Liberal Arts Hall. The courtyard has an archway and a grand staircase that lead up to it from the Quarter Mile.","https://ritpedia.rit.edu/Eastman_Kodak_Quad",[1352],{"_70":1348,"_72":1353,"_45":1347,"_74":1346},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/quad_courtyards_eastman_kodak_quad.jpg",{"_43":1370,"_45":1371,"_47":1372,"_49":1373,"_235":1374,"_63":64,"_65":1370,"_67":1375},{"_32":684,"_39":1356},[1357],[1358,1359,1360,1361,1362],[1363,1364],[1368,1369],[1367,1366],[1365,1366],[1363,1364],-77.681518,43.084981,-77.681529,43.084824,-77.680837,-77.680842,43.084988,3739,1022,"Destler and Johnson Quad","A large and peaceful quad celebrating President Bill Destler and Rebecca Johnson.","A beautiful quad between Louise Slaughter Hall and Sustainability Institute Hall, dedicated in May 2017 in honor of President Bill Destler and his spouse, Rebecca Johnson.",[1376],{"_70":1372,"_72":1377,"_45":1371,"_74":1370},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/quads_courtyards_destler_and_johnson_quad.jpg",{"_43":1394,"_45":1395,"_47":1396,"_49":1396,"_235":1397,"_51":1398,"_63":64,"_65":1394,"_67":1399},{"_32":684,"_39":1380},[1381],[1382,1383,1384,1385,1386],[1387,1388],[1393,1388],[1391,1392],[1389,1390],[1387,1388],-77.677226,43.084299,-77.677242,43.084162,-77.676797,43.084142,-77.676786,3743,1023,"Infinity Quad","The Infinity Quad is a quadrangle on the academic side of the RIT campus. It was part of the original construction of the Henrietta campus. It is known as the 'Infinity' Quad because of the sculpture that looks like a mobius strip.","https://ritpedia.rit.edu/Infinity_Quad",[1400],{"_70":1396,"_72":1401,"_45":1395,"_74":1394},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/quads_courtyards_infinity_quad.jpg",{"_43":1417,"_45":1418,"_47":1419,"_49":1420,"_63":64,"_65":1417,"_67":1421},{"_32":684,"_39":1404},[1405],[1406,1407,1408,1409,1410],[1411,1412],[1416,1412],[1415,1414],[1413,1414],[1411,1412],-77.668305,43.085132,-77.668297,43.084693,-77.667699,-77.667696,4531,1312,"Central Quad","Quad between DSP, Colby, and Fish res halls",[],{"_43":1439,"_45":1440,"_47":1441,"_49":1442,"_63":64,"_65":1439,"_67":1443},{"_32":684,"_39":1424},[1425],[1426,1427,1428,1429,1430],[1431,1432],[1437,1438],[1435,1436],[1433,1434],[1431,1432],-77.668777,43.084582,-77.66878,43.084186,-77.668181,43.08418,-77.668179,43.084588,4535,1313,"Clock-Tower Quad","Quad between Kate Gleason, Colby, and Baker Halls B/C/D",[],{"_43":1475,"_45":1476,"_47":574,"_49":1477,"_235":1478,"_51":1479,"_63":64,"_65":1475,"_67":1480},{"_32":684,"_39":1446},[1447],[1448,1449,1450,1451,1452,1453,1454,1455,1456,1457],[1458,1459],[1473,1474],[1471,1472],[1469,1470],[1467,1468],[1465,1466],[1463,1464],[1460,1462],[1460,1461],[1458,1459],-77.680029,43.082777,-77.680024,43.082783,43.082951,-77.680137,43.082955,-77.680276,43.083098,-77.680627,43.083094,-77.680649,43.083029,-77.681078,43.083033,-77.681081,43.082781,2079,552,"Outdoor seating and entertainment area","Global Village is an internationally inspired, LEED-certified sustainable residential community and commercial complex located on RIT's campus. Open to both the public and RIT community, RIT's Global Village combines state-of-the-art student living with dining, shopping, learning, and event spaces to create a unified and modern upscale community. Global Village also hosts a number of convenient services including a post office, print center, and salon, as well as Shop One, RIT's acclaimed fine art and original craft gallery. RIT is committed to offering our students state-of-the-art housing, dining, and lifestyle options. Global Village provides a global environment for RIT students as they prepare to enter the global community, travel overseas, and join a culturally diverse workforce. To support this goal, and the entrepreneurial and global missions of RIT, each residential and commercial area represents different regions from around the world, giving students a global living experience along side their studies and time at RIT. Additionally, the entire complex and plaza supports year-round activities and events offering students a source of entertainment and community.","https://www.rit.edu/fa/globalvillage/about",[1481],{"_70":574,"_72":1482,"_45":1476,"_74":1475},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/400_gvp_gvplazamappic.jpg",223,"Quads And Courtyards",60,{"_43":1631,"_47":1632,"_32":126,"_127":-5,"_128":-5,"_129":1633,"_130":131,"_132":133},[1488,1489,1490,1491,1492,1493,1494,1495,1496,1497],{"_32":33,"_34":1617,"_36":1618},{"_32":33,"_34":1603,"_36":1604},{"_32":33,"_34":1589,"_36":1590},{"_32":33,"_34":1575,"_36":1576},{"_32":33,"_34":1561,"_36":1562},{"_32":33,"_34":1549,"_36":1550},{"_32":33,"_34":1537,"_36":1538},{"_32":33,"_34":1525,"_36":1526},{"_32":33,"_34":1510,"_36":1511},{"_32":33,"_34":1498,"_36":1499},{"_43":1503,"_45":1504,"_47":1505,"_49":1506,"_235":1507,"_53":396,"_55":397,"_57":86,"_63":64,"_65":1508,"_67":1509},{"_32":38,"_39":1500},[1501,1502],-77.674223,43.083957,5743,2651,"Frederick Douglass Sculpture","Created by Olivia Kim, an adjunct professor at RIT","The Frederick Douglass sculpture was created by Olivia Kim, an adjunct professor at RIT who teaches figure sculpture for the illustrator department. The sculpture was commissioned by RIT President David Munson and Vice President and Associate Provost for Diversity and Inclusion Keith Jenkins in celebration of the 50th anniversary of RIT's Black Awareness Coordinating Committee (BACC).",6415,[],{"_43":1515,"_45":1516,"_47":1517,"_49":1518,"_235":1519,"_51":1520,"_53":1203,"_55":1204,"_59":1521,"_63":64,"_65":1515,"_67":1522},{"_32":38,"_39":1512},[1513,1514],-77.67698,43.08356,4615,1334,"Principia","Inviting the RIT community and visitors to contemplate the scope, history, and beauty of science and math.","Principia, by Larry Kirkland | Mural, 1999 Etched, polished black granite, 15x25","https://www.rit.edu/science/sites/rit.edu.science/files/Atrium%20Floor%20pamphlet.pdf","Bruce & Nora James Atrium",[1523],{"_70":1517,"_72":1524,"_45":1516,"_74":1515},"https://www.rit.edu/news/umag/fall2004/urls/Gallery6.jpg",{"_43":1530,"_45":1531,"_47":1532,"_49":1533,"_63":64,"_65":1530,"_67":1534},{"_32":38,"_39":1527},[1528,1529],-77.679146,43.085514,3791,1037,"Lighted RIT Sign","Large, lighted RIT sign on top of Institute Hall.",[1535],{"_70":1532,"_72":1536,"_45":1531,"_74":1530},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/rit_sign.jpg",{"_43":1542,"_45":1543,"_47":1544,"_49":1545,"_63":64,"_65":1542,"_67":1546},{"_32":38,"_39":1539},[1540,1541],-77.67288,43.084133,3787,1036,"Painted Rocks","Large rocks colorfully painted by students.",[1547],{"_70":1544,"_72":1548,"_45":1543,"_74":1542},"http://www.rit.edu/emcs/admissions/bca/urls/stories/blogs/pjs8419/breeze4.jpg",{"_43":1554,"_45":1555,"_47":1556,"_49":1557,"_63":64,"_65":1554,"_67":1558},{"_32":38,"_39":1551},[1552,1553],-77.678375,43.08321,3783,1035,"Fountain","A popular meeting spot.",[1559],{"_70":1556,"_72":1560,"_45":1555,"_74":1554},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/fountain.jpg",{"_43":1566,"_45":1567,"_47":1568,"_49":1569,"_235":1570,"_51":1571,"_63":64,"_65":1566,"_67":1572},{"_32":38,"_39":1563},[1564,1565],-77.67838,43.08533,3779,1034,"Unity","Unity, by Juan Carlos Caballero-Perez, is a sculpture located in the Unity Quad between Booth Hall, the Center for Bioscience Education and Technology, and Institute Hall.","This sculpture, sited between the College of Imaging Arts and Sciences, the new College of Applied Science and Technology and the College of Engineering is aptly named Unity. The work is the result of a collaboration between two RIT faculty members in the metals program of the School for American Crafts: Juan Carlos Caballero-Perez and Leonard Urso. The sculpture is composed of three individual sections, with the tallest at 24 feet. According to the artists, each piece stands individually, yet they are a family of sculptures that work as a symbolic whole. The three sections represent the unity of science, technology and art at RIT as well as alluding to the entire university, the College of Imaging Arts and Sciences, and the School for American Crafts. The theme of unity is further echoed in the materials; the silver stainless steel , basic to many products of technology, contrasts with the marks on the surface, which refer back to the hand of the artist. To create the work Caballero-Perez and Urso started with rough sketches, and then worked through a series of 3-d models made from cut-out pieces of cardboard. Once the final model was completed the actual work started to take shape. The piece was constructed off-campus at the Mahaney Welding Supply Company, owned by RIT alumni Mike Krupnicki. A telescoping pipe system serves as the skeleton, and engineer had to approve the final structure.","https://www.rit.edu/artoncampus/unity",[1573],{"_70":1568,"_72":1574,"_45":1567,"_74":1566},"http://artoncampus.rit.edu/urls/art/CAST_Statue_2.jpg2.jpg",{"_43":1580,"_45":1581,"_47":1582,"_49":1583,"_235":1584,"_51":1585,"_63":64,"_65":1580,"_67":1586},{"_32":38,"_39":1577},[1578,1579],-77.67699,43.084236,1359,364,"Construction 105","Colloquially, the infinity symbol or infinity statue, is a sculpture of a 3-sided mobius strip which was installed when the Henrietta campus opened in 1968.","Sculpture formally know as Construction #105 was built in 1968 by Jose de Rivera. It resembles a mobius strip and is on the academic side of the RIT campus. It sits in the center of the Infinity Quad and marks the Academic end of the Quarter Mile. It is called the \"Infinity Symbol\" because, at certain angles during its rotation, it makes a near-perfect sideways infinity symbol. Stainless steel and black granite - 19' x 8' x 2 1/2'.","https://www.rit.edu/artoncampus/construction-105",[1587],{"_70":1582,"_72":1588,"_45":1581,"_74":1580},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/infinity_quad.jpg",{"_43":1594,"_45":1595,"_47":1596,"_49":1597,"_235":1598,"_51":1599,"_63":64,"_65":1594,"_67":1600},{"_32":38,"_39":1591},[1592,1593],-77.669174,43.084354,1355,362,"Sundial","Sculpture marking the Residential side end of the Quarter Mile.","Built in 1968, the Sundial, by Alistair Bevington is a sculpture on the residential side of the RIT campus. It sits at an important intersection North of Grace Watson Hall and the East end of the beginning of the Quarter Mile. Steel and stainless steel. 18' x 25' x 14'","http://artoncampus.rit.edu/art/43/",[1601],{"_70":1596,"_72":1602,"_45":1595,"_74":1594},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/041_bevington.jpg",{"_43":1608,"_45":1609,"_47":1610,"_49":1611,"_235":1612,"_51":1613,"_63":64,"_65":1608,"_67":1614},{"_32":38,"_39":1605},[1606,1607],-77.678821,43.083127,1347,360,"Tiger Statue","The tiger statue is a representation of Spirit, the Bengal tiger cub RIT adopted as its first mascot in 1963.","The Bronzed Bengal Tiger Statue located on the Quarter Mile, across from the Eastman Quad, was created by sculptor Duff Wehle. The tiger statue is a representation of Spirit, the Bengal tiger cub RIT adopted as its first mascot in 1963. The statue was commissioned by RIT students and made its debut on campus on November 10, 1989. Since then, it has been an important landmark at RIT, serving as a meeting place, photo prop and guardian of the Quarter Mile. Despite years of typical wear and tear, the statue has not lost any of its defining features and looks just as good today as it did back in 1989.","https://www.rit.edu/artoncampus/rit-bengal-tiger",[1615],{"_70":1610,"_72":1616,"_45":1609,"_74":1608},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/wehle_tiger_2.jpg",{"_43":1622,"_45":1623,"_47":1624,"_49":1625,"_235":1626,"_51":1627,"_63":64,"_65":1622,"_67":1628},{"_32":38,"_39":1619},[1620,1621],-77.67438,43.08466,1335,357,"Sentinel","Designed by eminent sculptor, Albert Paley, the 'Sentinel' is an iconic metal structure amid the \"brick city\" of RIT.","The Sentinel, built by Albert Paley for RIT in 2003, is the largest sculpture on any American university campus. Weighing in at 110 tons, this monumental structure dominates the RIT skyline. As Paley's most ambitious commission to date, he referred \"to the technological dimension of the Institute and the dynamic transformative nature of the educational process.\" In the 1960s there was an early architectural rendering during the planning stages of RIT's new campus in Henrietta, NY. The original plans showed a pair of towering brick monoliths at the entrance to the Institute, in keeping with the starkly brutalist vision of the original architectural plan. However by the time the new campus was completed in 1968, the monoliths had disappeared. They were not replaced until 35 years later when The Sentinel was installed in the newly redesigned plaza. Steel, stainless steel, and bronze - 73' x 30' x 30'.","https://www.rit.edu/artoncampus/sundial",[1629],{"_70":1624,"_72":1630,"_45":1623,"_74":1622},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/sentinel.jpg",219,"Landmarks",59,{"_43":1898,"_47":1899,"_32":126,"_127":-5,"_128":-5,"_129":1900,"_130":131,"_132":133},[1636,1637,1638,1639,1640,1641,1642,1643,1644,1645,1646,1647,1648,1649],{"_32":33,"_34":1852,"_36":1853},{"_32":33,"_34":1836,"_36":1837},{"_32":33,"_34":1819,"_36":1820},{"_32":33,"_34":1806,"_36":1807},{"_32":33,"_34":1790,"_36":1791},{"_32":33,"_34":1776,"_36":1777},{"_32":33,"_34":1763,"_36":1764},{"_32":33,"_34":1749,"_36":1750},{"_32":33,"_34":1731,"_36":1732},{"_32":33,"_34":1719,"_36":1720},{"_32":33,"_34":1703,"_36":1704},{"_32":33,"_34":1685,"_36":1686},{"_32":33,"_34":1666,"_36":1667},{"_32":33,"_34":1650,"_36":1651},{"_43":1654,"_45":1655,"_47":1656,"_49":1657,"_53":1658,"_55":1659,"_57":58,"_59":1660,"_61":1661,"_63":64,"_65":1662,"_67":1663},{"_32":38,"_39":1652},[1653,282],-77.66839,7001,2888,"BakerFIT","24 hour fitness space","BHB","029","A133","24 hours",6920,[1664],{"_70":1656,"_72":1665,"_45":1655,"_74":1654},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/BakerFIT_A-133.jpg",{"_43":1671,"_45":1672,"_47":1673,"_49":1674,"_235":1675,"_534":1676,"_51":1677,"_53":1678,"_55":1679,"_59":1680,"_61":1681,"_63":64,"_65":1671,"_67":1682},{"_32":38,"_39":1668},[1669,1670],-77.67219,43.08421,623,174,"Student Health Center","Health care, support, and education for students","The Student Health Center provides health care, support and education for students. Professional staff are here not only to take care of you when you are sick, but also to help you learn to prevent illness and maintain good health.","585-475-2255","https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/studenthealth/","AUG","023","1100","<strong>During Academic Year:</strong> <table> <tr><td>Monday - Thursday</td><td> 8 a.m. - 6:30 p.m.</td></tr> <tr><td>Friday</td><td> 8 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.</td></tr> </table> <strong>Summer & Academic Breaks:</strong> <table></br> <tr><td>Monday - Friday</td><td> 8 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.</td></tr> </table>",[1683],{"_70":1673,"_72":1684,"_45":1672,"_74":1671},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/023a_aug_shc.jpg",{"_43":1690,"_45":1691,"_47":1692,"_49":1693,"_235":1694,"_534":1695,"_51":1696,"_53":396,"_55":397,"_59":1697,"_61":1698,"_63":64,"_65":1690,"_67":1699},{"_32":38,"_39":1687},[1688,1689],-77.67464,43.084244,647,181,"Disability Services Office - DSO","Providing equal access to programs, services, and physical facilities to students with disabilities","We strive to foster an environment where students and faculty/staff with disabilities are welcomed, valued and respected.</br>The DSO reviews requests for academic adjustments related to students' disabilities and medical conditions. We are guided by the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 which protects individuals with disabilities from discrimination.","585-475-2023","https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/disabilityservices/","1150","Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.",[1700],{"_70":1701,"_72":1702,"_45":1691,"_74":1690},"Disability Services Office","https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/disabilityservices/sites/rit.edu.studentaffairs.disabilityservices/files/8.jpg",{"_43":1707,"_45":1708,"_47":1709,"_49":1710,"_235":1711,"_534":1712,"_51":1713,"_53":1678,"_55":1679,"_59":1714,"_61":1715,"_63":64,"_65":1707,"_67":1716},{"_32":38,"_39":1705},[1706,1670],-77.672066,651,182,"Counseling and Psychological Services","Free, confidential, and personalized services to meet the mental health needs of currently enrolled undergraduate and graduate students attending the RIT Main campus","Free, confidential, and personalized services to meet the mental health needs of currently enrolled undergraduates and graduate students attending the RIT Main campus.</br> Counseling and Psychological Services offers primarily individual psychotherapy, but also includes group counseling, crisis intervention, and referrals to outside resources to help students change and thrive as they navigate the daily challenges of college life.","585-475-2261","https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/counseling/","2100","Monday - Friday 9:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.",[1717],{"_70":1709,"_72":1718,"_45":1708,"_74":1707},"https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/counseling/sites/rit.edu.studentaffairs.counseling/files/slideshow_urls/urlv4.jpg",{"_43":1723,"_45":1724,"_47":1725,"_49":1726,"_235":1727,"_534":150,"_51":1728,"_53":166,"_55":167,"_57":267,"_59":288,"_61":150,"_63":64,"_65":1729,"_67":1730},{"_32":38,"_39":1721},[976,1722],43.084167,655,183,"Women, Gender, and Sexuality Resource Center","Advocacy, Education, and Celebration for the RIT community","The Women, Gender, and Sexuality Resource Center provides advocacy, education, and celebration for RIT community members of all genders, gender identities, and sexual orientations.\r\nOur vision is to promote an inclusive campus community that is safe, equitable, respectful of all members, and acknowledges the needs of our intersectional identities. Our team will continue to evolve our services and programming to meet the needs of our dynamic student population.","https://www.rit.edu/studentlife/women-gender-and-sexuality-resource-center",1499,[],{"_43":1736,"_45":1737,"_47":1738,"_49":1739,"_235":1740,"_534":1741,"_51":1742,"_53":1743,"_55":1744,"_61":1745,"_63":64,"_65":1736,"_67":1746},{"_32":38,"_39":1733},[1734,1735],-77.672554,43.08501,2063,548,"Judson-Hale Aquatics Center","The recreation area pool includes a current channel, vortex, bubble jets, water basketball/volleyball, and a 20 person hot tub.","The facility includes two pools: a competition pool and a leisure pool. The competition pool is an eight-lane, 25-yard pool, set at approximately 80 degrees. The Judson Competition Pool also includes a separate diving well with two one-meter and two three-meter diving boards. The Hale Recreation Pool includes a vortex and a hot tub which seats approximately 25 people.","585-475-2367","http://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/ciar/facilities_indoor.php#Aquatics","GOR","024","<a href=\"http://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/ciar/facilities_schedules.php#pool\">Hours of Operation</a>",[1747],{"_70":1738,"_72":1748,"_45":1737,"_74":1736},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/024_gor_comppool.jpg",{"_43":1753,"_45":1754,"_47":1755,"_49":1756,"_235":1757,"_51":1758,"_53":1743,"_55":1744,"_61":1759,"_63":64,"_65":1753,"_67":1760},{"_32":38,"_39":1751},[1752,1621],-77.67271,2067,549,"Wiedman Fitness Center","A two-story, 16,000 square foot facility featuring a full range of selectorized machines, free weights, cardiovascular equipment, and a large stretching area.","The Wiedman Fitness Center is a two-story area that is 16,000 square feet and features a full range of state of the art equipment. Included are treadmills, ellipticals, step mills, a variety of stationary and spinning bikes, selectorized resistance machines, free weights, multiple adjustable and stationary benches, abdominal training stations, exercise weighted balls and exercise balls, large stretching areas, power lifting stations and multi-station lifting areas. Along with this wide variety of equipment, the Fitness Center also provides the following general services: free nutritional counseling, student attendants to provide basic usage information for the fitness equipment, personal training courses for students (through the Wellness Instructional Program), and personal training services for faculty and staff (through the faculty staff Better Me program).","http://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/ciar/facilities_indoor.php#Fitness","<a href=\"http://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/ciar/facilities_schedules.php#slcfh\">Hours of Operation</a>",[1761],{"_70":1755,"_72":1762,"_45":1754,"_74":1753},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/024_gor_weightroom.jpg",{"_43":1768,"_45":1769,"_47":1770,"_49":1771,"_235":1772,"_63":64,"_65":1768,"_67":1773},{"_32":38,"_39":1765},[1766,1767],-77.68261,43.08566,3671,1001,"Family Medicine Practice","Primary Care Right on Campus","Complete Care in a Convenient Location. Our practice offers comprehensive healthcare services close to home -- and even closer to work. We see community residents and RIT faculty and staff(and their families). For inquires or to make an appointment, call us at 585 922 3100.  Interpreter services are available. We accept most insurance plans, including Medicare and Medicaid.",[1774],{"_70":1770,"_72":1775,"_45":1769,"_74":1768},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/078_sla_fmp.jpg",{"_43":1781,"_45":1782,"_47":1783,"_49":1784,"_235":1785,"_51":1786,"_57":86,"_63":64,"_65":1781,"_67":1787},{"_32":38,"_39":1778},[1779,1780],-77.68124,43.08272,3751,1026,"Wellness Center Gym (GV)","The Global Village Wellness Center is available to faculty and staff via swipe access 24/7.","The Global Village Wellness Center is available to faculty and staff via swipe access 24/7. The facility includes a small fitness area, exercise studio and locker rooms. Individuals are welcome to use the studio any time fitness classes are not in session. All faculty and staff have free use of two excellent fitness facilities: the Student Life Center (SLC) and the Global Village Wellness Center. Your RIT faculty/staff I.D. is all you need to gain access to either one. Present your I.D. to the reception desk at the SLC during regular operating hours. You also have the ability to get a locker, towel, and a variety of sports equipment free of charge.","https://www.rit.edu/fa/betterme/get-moving/fitness-facilities-recreation",[1788],{"_70":1783,"_72":1789,"_45":1782,"_74":1781},"https://www.rit.edu/fa/betterme/sites/rit.edu.fa.betterme/files//urls/gv-lr.jpg",{"_43":1795,"_45":1796,"_47":1797,"_49":1798,"_235":1799,"_51":1800,"_53":1801,"_55":1679,"_57":86,"_59":1802,"_63":64,"_65":1795,"_67":1803},{"_32":38,"_39":1792},[1793,1794],-77.67196,43.084526,3759,1028,"Hale-Andrews Student Life Center: Main Office","Management of RIT recreation facilities and support for recreation services and memberships","The Hale-Andrews Student Life Center Main Office supports recreation facilities management and support for recreation services and memberships.","https://www.rit.edu/~w-criw/","HAC","First Floor",[1804],{"_70":1797,"_72":1805,"_45":1796,"_74":1795},"https://www.rit.edu/~w-criw/urls/criw_logo_new.jpg",{"_43":1810,"_45":1811,"_47":1812,"_49":1813,"_235":1814,"_51":1815,"_63":64,"_65":1810,"_67":1816},{"_32":38,"_39":1808},[1047,1809],43.085007,4611,1333,"Ritter Public Skate - Rentals","The arena is a venue for public recreation skating, figure skating classes, and ice hockey.","Bring your friends and family to the Riter Ice Arena for some ice skating fun! Public skate hours are available for members of the RIT community and the general public. See our website for hours, fees, and services.","https://www.rit.edu/fa/arenas/ritter-arena/public-skate",[1817],{"_70":1812,"_72":1818,"_45":1811,"_74":1810},"https://www.rit.edu/fa/arenas/sites/rit.edu.fa.arenas/files/pubskate2.jpg",{"_43":1823,"_45":1824,"_47":1825,"_49":1826,"_235":1827,"_534":1828,"_51":1829,"_53":1830,"_55":1831,"_59":1832,"_61":1833,"_63":64,"_65":1823,"_67":1834},{"_32":38,"_39":1821},[1822,1593],-77.684746,4787,1385,"Red Barn Climbing Gym","One of the top collegiate indoor rock climbing facilities in the country.","RBC is a bouldering-only gym, where climbs are shorter and falls are protected with padding. Climbing routes are set and maintained to accommodate all abilities and skill levels, from beginner to expert.<strong>All non-RIT visitors must be 18 years of age or older.</strong></br>The Red Barn is a 100 year old \"Wells\" style dairy barn that lacks many modern amenities such as heat and plumbing. Please dress based on the outside temperature. There is a \"Port-A-John\" located in the main parking lot that is available to all visitors.</br></br>RBC is open when RIT semester classes are in session and closed during exam weeks and breaks.","(585) 292-6571","https://www.rit.edu/~w-criw/outdoor-rockclimbing.php","RED","080","Barn","<strong>Semester Hours: </strong> <table> <tr><td>Monday - Friday</td><td> 5:00 PM - 10:00 PM</td></tr> <tr><td>Saturday</td><td> 1:00 PM - 10:00 PM</td></tr> <tr><td>Sunday</td><td> 1:00 PM - 6:00 PM</td></tr> </table>",[1835],{"_70":1825,"_72":1830,"_45":1824,"_74":1823},{"_43":1841,"_45":1842,"_47":1843,"_49":1844,"_235":1845,"_534":1846,"_51":1847,"_53":1678,"_55":1679,"_59":1848,"_63":64,"_65":1841,"_67":1849},{"_32":38,"_39":1838},[1839,1840],-77.672,43.08416,4903,1890,"Case Management","Support for navigating on and off campus health and wellness services","The Case Management team assists students in navigating health and wellness services both on and off campus.","585-475-3963","https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/wellness/case-management","2914",[1850],{"_70":1843,"_72":1851,"_45":1842,"_74":1841},"https://www.rit.edu/studentaffairs/wellness/sites/rit.edu.studentaffairs.wellness/files/iStock-666600116.jpg",{"_43":1891,"_45":1892,"_47":1893,"_235":1894,"_53":1801,"_55":1679,"_63":64,"_65":1891,"_67":1895},{"_32":684,"_39":1854},[1855],[1856,1857,1858,1859,1860,1861,1862,1863,1864,1865,1866,1867,1868],[1869,1870],[1889,1890],[1887,1888],[1885,1886],[1883,1884],[1877,1882],[1880,1881],[1879,1878],[1877,1878],[1875,1876],[1873,1874],[1871,1872],[1869,1870],-77.672854,43.084809,-77.671148,43.084835,-77.671149,43.084683,-77.671081,43.084685,-77.671079,43.084604,-77.670988,-77.670987,43.084468,43.084465,-77.671075,43.084383,-77.672113,43.084368,-77.672114,43.084332,-77.67284,43.084323,115,29,"Hale-Andrews Student Life Center","The first of the buildings in RIT's athletics and wellness cluster, the SLC serves the recreational and wellness instruction needs of the RIT community. The Center includes five multi-purpose courts, a dance and aerobics studio, an elevated 1/8 mile running track, conference and classroom space. The Center also serves as the main office site for RIT's Center for Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation.",[1896],{"_70":1893,"_72":1897,"_45":1892,"_74":1891},"https://maps.rit.edu/pictures/023_hac.jpg",215,"Health Wellness",58,{"_43":2206,"_47":1944,"_32":126,"_127":-5,"_128":-5,"_129":2207,"_130":131,"_132":133},[1903,1904,1905,1906,1907,1908,1909,1910,1911,1912,1913,1914,1915,1916,1917,1918,1919,1920,